Third-party attributions
------------------------------------------------------------------------

Byte-pattern signatures, hook strategies, and native-dispatcher
resolution for GTA IV Complete Edition 1.2.0.59 are derived from or
inspired by:

  GTAIV.EFLC.FusionFix
    https://github.com/ThirteenAG/GTAIV.EFLC.FusionFix
    Copyright (C) its contributors.
    Licensed under GNU General Public License v3.0.

Native-function hashes, struct layouts, and historical offset tables
are derived from:

  Zolika1351/iv-sdk
    https://github.com/Zolika1351/iv-sdk
    Historical reference for GTA IV 1.0.7.0 / 1.0.8.0 natives.

The GTA IV AES-256 key SHA-1 fingerprint (20 bytes) embedded in
common/keys_iv.cpp as kAesKeySha1Hex is the published fingerprint
used by several open-source IV tools, including:

  ReneSchimmelpfennig/GTA-IV-PS3Decode
    https://github.com/ReneSchimmelpfennig/GTA-IV-PS3Decode
    (tools/rpf3.py, KEY_SHA1 constant)

No key bytes are shipped. The fingerprint only identifies the 32-byte
key material inside the user's own GTAIV.exe at run time. The IMG v3
on-disk layout driving common/img_v3.cpp was cross-checked against
GTAIV.EFLC.FusionFix's imgloader.ixx (which stores the key itself
inline in its binary; we do not) and against the independent format
notes in ReneSchimmelpfennig/GTA-IV-PS3Decode. The AES-256 and SHA-1
implementations in common/aes.cpp and common/sha1.cpp are clean-room
from NIST FIPS-197 and RFC 3174 respectively.

Any direct source lifts from the above projects are tagged with inline
`[FusionFix: path:line]` comments at the lift site. Code marked that way
is covered by its originating project's copyright and license. This
project's own code is covered by its own GPL-3.0 grant above; the
combined work ships as GPL-3.0.
